# Ticket 001 – User Cannot Log In

**Category:** User Account / Authentication  
**Environment:** Windows 11 VM  
**Status:** Resolved

## Issue
User reported that they could not complete the normal Windows login process.

## Investigation
I opened Local Users and Groups using `lusrmgr.msc` and checked the user's account properties.

The account was configured with **User must change password at next logon**.

## Resolution
The user signed in with their existing credentials and was prompted to create a new password.

## Verification
The password change completed successfully and the user was able to access Windows.

## What I Learned
A login problem does not automatically mean that the password needs to be reset. Checking the account configuration first can identify the actual cause and avoid unnecessary changes.
